  "reason": "RNA-only scvi multiprofile is currently the strongest direction (0.650-0.653 accuracy), while the only multimodal test (scvi + resnet50, avgpool, concat) is slightly below RNA-only at 0.632 and image-only resnet50 is weak at 0.328. The main unresolved question is whether the multimodal underperformance is due to naive concatenation fusion. config_031 changes only fusion from concat to weighted relative to config_030, directly testing whether adaptive fusion can allow the image modality to help without changing the already informative RNA encoder, profile, or aggregation. This is a minimal, high-value comparison for deciding whether multimodal fusion is worth further exploration."
